  "title": "The timeline notices it is full of banh mi",
  "summary": "From Fri 13 Nov to the end of the window, cluster members and people around them posted about banh mi every day: announcing they would get one, announcing they would not, posting photos, and remarking on how many such posts there were. Several posts are about the wave itself (\"a psyop to get me to order a banh mi\", \"out of control\", \"inexplicable\"). One member joined in with a different Vietnamese dish. One reported a Vietnamese restaurant with no banh mi on the menu. One asked whether a burrito is a kind of banh mi and was told two days later that a banh mi is a hot dog. A small account announced an order, said to brace for a picture, and 29 minutes later posted it.",
